# WASM DE1 — hello fold is only let greet then println ident

File: openOODA/audit/wasm_de1.oot
DE1 proof. Re-read ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fold.oo. Main match is still
the exact hello.oo shape. Did not edit wasm_emit_fold.oo.
Did not edit wasm_emit.oo.

Logline: wasm_fold_hello returns the greet line only when fn main is let IDENT = greet(STRING); println(IDENT); then RBRACE.
Setup: tokenize_lines packs kind in field 0 and unquoted text in field 3.
Beats:
  1. After the main LBRACE, accept only KW_LET IDENT EQ IDENT greet LPAREN STRING RPAREN, optional SEMI, IDENT println LPAREN that IDENT RPAREN, optional SEMI, then RBRACE.
  2. Extra statements miss. A no-let println(greet(...)) misses. A typed let misses.
  3. hello.oo matches and folds main's STRING. Hostile extra println misses.

## 1. Exact main match

  ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fold.oo is 190 lines. Under 256.
  Public helper is wasm_fold_hello. Main match is wf_main_greet_arg.
  Main has no skip-to-return walk. Each kind is a hard gate.

    KW_LET IDENT vname EQ IDENT greet LPAREN STRING RPAREN SEMI
    IDENT println LPAREN IDENT vname RPAREN SEMI RBRACE

  After LBRACE the next kind must be KW_LET. A leading println misses.
  After the IDENT, the next kind must be EQ. A COLON type mark misses.
  After EQ the kind must be IDENT greet, then LPAREN STRING RPAREN.
  An IDENT arg, a missing call, or a second greet arg misses.
  After the optional let SEMI the next ident must be println.
  println is IDENT. It is not a keyword. The text must be println.
  The println arg must be the same vname. A STRING misses.
  A different ident misses.
  After the optional println SEMI the next kind must be RBRACE.
  A second println is IDENT, not RBRACE. Extra stmts miss.

  wasm_fold_hello then needs greet body return STRING + param + STRING.
  Fold text is prefix + main STRING + suffix.
  An empty STRING arg has length 0. wasm_fold_hello returns "".

  The match is still exact. The file is not broken. No edit.

## 2. hello.oo matches

  fixtures/hello.oo main body:

    let message = greet("openOODA Developer");
    println(message);

  Lexer skips // comments. They are not tokens.
  After main LBRACE the kinds are:

    KW_LET IDENT message EQ IDENT greet LPAREN STRING RPAREN SEMI
    IDENT println LPAREN IDENT message RPAREN SEMI RBRACE

  vname is message. greet arg is openOODA Developer.
  println arg is message. Next token is RBRACE.
  wf_main_greet_arg returns openOODA Developer.

  greet body after its LBRACE:

    KW_RETURN STRING Hello,  PLUS IDENT name PLUS STRING ! SEMI RBRACE

  Result: Hello,  + openOODA Developer + ! .
  That is Hello, openOODA Developer!
  Lock: scripts/wasm_hello_smoke.oo.

  Sibling INT scratch on this host (cwd ooda/, same product binary):

    /tmp/grok-goal-3afece913704/implementer/int_proof.log

  emit-wasm fixtures/hello.oo EXIT 0. 197 bytes. Magic 00 61 73 6d.
  Bytes name fd_write and Hello, openOODA Developer!.
  wasmtime prints Hello, openOODA Developer! and exits 0.

## 3. Extra println misses

  fixtures/wasm_hello_hostile.oo main:

    let message = greet("openOODA Developer");
    println(message);
    println("other");

  After the first println SEMI the next kind is IDENT.
  That IDENT text is println. It is not RBRACE.
  wf_main_greet_arg returns "". wasm_fold_hello returns "".
  emit-wasm must not plant a greet-only print on main.
  Lock: scripts/wasm_hello_hostile_smoke.oo.

  wasm_emit.oo applies fold first, and only when the name is main.
  Empty fold does not call oo_wasm_set_fn_print for the greet line.
  greet is not main. greet keeps dummy end.
  Hostile main is not one println(STRING). Later print helpers miss.
  Extra println still misses.

## 4. No-let and typed let miss

  fixtures/wasm_hello_nolet.oo main:

    println(greet("x"));

  After LBRACE the kind is IDENT, not KW_LET. Return is "".
  Fold does not take Hello, x!.

  A typed let is KW_LET IDENT COLON. The next kind must be EQ.
  COLON misses.

## 5. Fold uses main arg, not verify

  hello.oo verify tokens start with KW_VERIFY IDENT greet.
  wf_find_fn wants KW_FN then IDENT. verify is unused.
  First greet(STRING) in the file is World. This match never leaves main.
  A first-call scan would take World. Fold does not.

